#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "ATProtoSocial (Bluesky) Integration"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "TWBlue now supports the AT Protocol (ATProto), the decentralized social networking protocol that powers Bluesky. This allows you to interact with your Bluesky account directly within TWBlue."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Adding an ATProtoSocial Account"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "To connect your Bluesky account to TWBlue, you will need your user **handle** and an **App Password**."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "User Handle"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "This is your unique Bluesky identifier, often in the format ``@username.bsky.social`` or a custom domain you've configured (e.g., ``@yourname.com``)."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "App Password"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Bluesky uses App Passwords for third-party applications like TWBlue instead of your main account password. You need to generate an App Password from your Bluesky account settings."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Go to Bluesky Settings (usually accessible from the Bluesky app or website)."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Navigate to the \"App passwords\" section (this might be under \"Advanced\" or \"Security\")."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Generate a new App Password. Give it a descriptive name (e.g., \"TWBlue\")."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Copy the generated App Password immediately. It will usually only be shown once."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Once you have your handle and the App Password:"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Open TWBlue and go to the Session Manager (Application Menu -> Manage accounts)."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Click on \"New account\"."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Select \"ATProtoSocial (Bluesky)\" from the menu."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "A dialog will prompt you to confirm that you want to authorize your account. Click \"Yes\"."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "You will then be asked for your Bluesky Handle. Enter your full handle (e.g., ``@username.bsky.social`` or ``username.bsky.social``)."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Next, you will be asked for the App Password you generated. Enter it carefully."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "If the credentials are correct, TWBlue will log in to your Bluesky account, and the new session will be added to your accounts list."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Key Features"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Once your ATProtoSocial account is connected, you can use the following features in TWBlue:"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Posting"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Create new posts (often called \"skeets\") with text, images, and specify language."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Timelines"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Home Timeline (Skyline)"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "View posts from users you follow."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "User Timelines"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "View posts from specific users."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Mentions & Replies"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "These will appear in your Notifications."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Notifications"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Receive notifications for likes, reposts, follows, mentions, replies, and quotes."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "User Actions"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Follow and unfollow users."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Mute and unmute users."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Block and unblock users (blocking is done on your PDS/server)."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Quoting Posts"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Quote other users' posts when you create a new post."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "User Search"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Search for users by their handle or display name."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Content Warnings"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Create posts with content warnings (sensitive content labels)."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Basic Concepts for ATProtoSocial"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/atprotosocial.rst
msgid "Further details on specific actions can be found in the relevant sections of this documentation. As Bluesky and the AT Protocol evolve, TWBlue will aim to incorporate new features and refinements."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/basic_concepts.rst
msgid "ATProtoSocial / Bluesky Specific Terms"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/basic_concepts.rst
msgid "When using the ATProtoSocial (Bluesky) integration, you might encounter these terms:"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/basic_concepts.rst
msgid "Handle"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/basic_concepts.rst
msgid "Your user-facing address on Bluesky (e.g., ``@username.bsky.social`` or a custom domain like ``@yourname.com``). This is what you use to log in with an App Password in TWBlue. Handles can be changed, but your DID remains the same."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/basic_concepts.rst
msgid "App Password"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/basic_concepts.rst
msgid "A specific password you generate within your Bluesky account settings (usually under Settings -> Advanced -> App passwords) for use with third-party applications like TWBlue. This is more secure than using your main account password, as each App Password can be revoked individually."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/basic_concepts.rst
msgid "DID (Decentralized Identifier)"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/basic_concepts.rst
msgid "A unique, permanent identifier for users and data on the AT Protocol. It typically starts with ``did:plc:``. Your DID doesn't change even if your handle does. You generally won't need to interact with DIDs directly in TWBlue, as handles are used more commonly for user interaction."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/basic_concepts.rst
msgid "Skyline"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/basic_concepts.rst
msgid "This is the term Bluesky uses for your main home timeline, showing posts from people you follow."
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/basic_concepts.rst
msgid "Skeet"
msgstr ""

#: documentation/source/basic_concepts.rst
msgid "An informal term for a post on Bluesky (akin to a \"tweet\" on Twitter)."
msgstr ""
